          "why_it_matters": "Hostetter turns a long period of musical life in Ethiopia into a solo instrument rather than a genre label: violin, looping and electronics carry Ethiopian melodic material through dub space, psychedelic texture and improvisation. The opening by Ethiopian artist Andy Betezema gives the Washington date an additional DMV connection without pretending the two sets are a collaboration. It is a small-room night about how instrumental technique can hold memory, place and cultural exchange at once.",
